When V8 receives JavaScript code, it works in two main phases:
1. Compilation phase (Memory Creation Phase)
2. Execution phase (Code Execution Phase)
=================================================================================================================================
Phase 1: Compilation (Memory Creation)
before executing the code , the engine will do below actions
🔹 Step 1: Parsing
    V8 reads the code
    Converts it into tokens
    Builds an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST)
  Ex:
  var a = 10;
  function foo() {}
  V8 understands:
  var → variable declaration
  function → function declaration

🔹 Step 2: Creating Execution Context - Memory Creation
📦 Memory is allocated for:
  Ex: var a	-> Memory created, value = undefined
  function foo()	-> Memory created, full function stored
  let / const	-> Memory created but kept uninitialized

This is what we call hoisting.
