Parsing:
Parsing = converting raw JavaScript text into a structure the engine can understand
Your code is just text:
var a = 10;
function foo() {
  console.log(a);
}
V8 cannot execute text directly.
So it converts it into three things:
Text → Tokens → AST (Abstract Syntax Tree)
2️⃣ Step 1.1 – Tokenization (Lexical Analysis)
V8 reads your code character by character.
Example:
var a = 10;

V8 breaks it into tokens:
Code	Token Type
var	  Keyword
a	    Identifier
=	    Assignment Operator
10	  Numeric Literal
;	    Statement End

So internally it becomes something like:
KEYWORD(var)
IDENTIFIER(a)
OPERATOR(=)
NUMBER(10)
⚠️ At this stage:
No memory
No execution
Only understanding grammar
